Fork base: abrensch/brouter commit 29898106b555e342ff3ade7ae3e9c1ae6644a43b.

Changes from upstream (Curvey modifications):
- brouter-core: added OsmTrack.CURVEY_FORK_MARKER (verifies fork changes reach Curvey).
- brouter-core: `continueStraight` is now an exact hard no-U-turn rule at via points. The leg that
  starts at a via point may not take its first step back along the edge the previous leg arrived on
  (`RoutingEngine.setReverseGuard`, `OsmPath`, `RoutingContext.reverseGuard*`). It replaces the former
  5 m no-go circle, which missed arrivals from farther away and stayed active for all later legs.
  A leg that cannot continue without turning around fails with
  "no track found ... (without a U-turn at <via>)" and does not feed the island detection (#200).
- brouter-core: new request key `arrivedfrom=lon,lat[|lon,lat...]` (`RoutingContext.arrivedFrom`, oldest
  first). With `continueStraight`, the first leg may not retrace the last listed position that is clear of
  the start (more than 2 m, engine metric). For callers that route leg by leg (#200; list form #204).
- brouter-core: new request key `driventrace=lon,lat,sigma|...` (`RoutingContext.drivenTrace`, oldest first,
  sigma = 1-sigma error in metres): where a vehicle was before the first waypoint (a reroute). With
  `continueStraight` and no `arrivedfrom`, `DrivenTraceMatcher` reconstructs the road path it drove with a
  hidden Markov map match (Viterbi over directed link positions; Gaussian emission, road-vs-straight distance
  transitions, turnarounds, outliers). The start moves onto the matched road when that is clearly more likely,
  and the first leg is guarded with the exact rule above when the direction is clearly known (no heading or
  angle is used). If the guarded first leg has no way forward, it is rerun without the guard: the vehicle turns
  around instead of getting no route. A planned via (`arrivedfrom`) still fails there. Replaces the earlier
  `drivenpath` key. Links the engine has frozen as islands are no match candidates (#204).
- brouter-core: rule R2 with `continueStraight`: a route step that runs backwards along the path before its leg
  (the matched driven trace, `arrivedfrom`, or the route so far at a via; its last 500 m, `DrivenTrace`) costs
  `reversalCostFactor` times its normal cost (distance cost, or time in the kinematic model; profile variable,
  default 5, 1 = off). A leg whose search fails with R2 on is searched again without it (`searchLeg`) (#204).
- brouter-mapaccess: `NodesCache.getSegmentFor` checks the waypoint matcher's type before using its dynamic
  range, so another `WaypointMatcher` implementation can collect links (#204).
- brouter-core: the no-U-turn guard (`continueStraight`) recognises a first step as going back when the
  arrival position lies on that step (`RoutingContext.isReverseGuardStep`), not only when the step ends at
  it. When the arrival began on the same stretch of road as the waypoint, the position is mid-road and the
  former exact-node comparison never fired, for `arrivedfrom` and the driven trace alike (#204).
- brouter-core: a leg counts as blocked by the no-U-turn guard only when the guard rejected a step
  (`RoutingContext.reverseGuardHit`); only then is island handling skipped and
  `ReverseGuardBlockedException` (message unchanged) raised. An armed guard that never fired no longer
  disables island recovery (#204).
- brouter-core: a planned via the no-U-turn guard cannot leave (a dead end for the profile) raises
  `ReverseGuardBlockedException` carrying that waypoint's index; `RoutingEngine.getReverseGuardBlockedWaypointIndex()`
  exposes it (-1 otherwise). The error message text is unchanged (#228).
- brouter-core: an unreachable waypoint (target/start island) now raises `UnreachableWaypointException`
  carrying the waypoint index; `RoutingEngine.getUnreachableWaypointIndex()` exposes it (-1 otherwise).
  The error message text is unchanged (#201).
- brouter-util: `BuildVersion.get()` reads the jar-manifest version that `OsmTrack.version` used to read
  directly, so a build without a manifest (the browser) can replace it. No behaviour change on the JVM.
- brouter-web (new module, Curvey web app #260): the engine compiled to WebAssembly (Wasm GC) with TeaVM.
  `JsFileSystem` serves `RandomAccessFile` reads from `globalThis.brouterFs`; `WebRouter` runs one request
  like Curvey's Android embedded engine. Browser replacements for `StackSampler` and `BuildVersion`. Only
  included in standalone builds, not when Curvey's Android app includes this repository.
